sentences.t:
ἠέ πῃ ἐς γαλόων ἢ εἰνατέρων ἐϋπέπλων
ἢ ἐς Ἀθηναίης ἐξοίχεται, ἔνθά περ ἄλλαι
Τρῳαὶ ἐϋπλόκαμοι δεινὴν θεὸν ἱλάσκονται;

sentences.tr:
ēe pēi es galoōn ē einaterōn eÿpeplōn
ē es Athēnaiēs exoichetai, entha per allai
Trōiai eÿplokamoi deinēn theon hilaskontai;

sentences.l:
“Strange man, your might will destroy you, and you do not pity
the childish child, and me, ill-fated, who soon a widow,
bereft of you, shall be;

for no longer any other
comfort will there be, when you have met your doom,
but griefs;

For indeed my father heavenly Achilles killed,
and sacked the city of the Cilicians, well-inhabited,
high-gated Thebe;

For three times, coming there, made trial the best men
around the two Ajaxes and renowned Idomeneus
and around the sons of Atreus and the valiant son of Tydeus;
